Why this is better than the old display

Old (N1/I1 bubbles) New (living landscape)
Abstract labels Spatial — you see where invasives cluster and where natives recover
One progress bar Three readouts — native cover, invasive cover, trajectory
Sliders' effects invisible Rainfall shifts soil colour, invasives cluster, effort plants natives, time shifts the whole canvas along the recovery gradient
Static Healthy plots shimmer gently — the landscape feels alive
No exploration Hover any plot for exact native/invasive/health percentages

The seeded RNG means each "Run Simulation" produces a fresh but plausible layout — no two runs look identical, yet the same slider settings always produce a consistent landscape (so learners can compare settings fairly).

